WEBVTT

1
00:47:45.986 --> 00:47:50.266
Are there any guests in the Open Church today? Give them a wave if you are here for the first time today.

2
00:47:50.266 --> 00:47:56.106
Don't be shy. Look over there, there's someone. Let's give a round of applause for all our guests in the church.

3
00:47:56.106 --> 00:47:58.466
You are welcome in the name of Jesus.

4
00:48:03.586 --> 00:48:11.866
Praise God. The Lord is truly risen. Shall we say that together one more time?

5
00:48:11.866 --> 00:48:18.706
The Lord is truly risen. One more time, okay? The Lord is truly risen.

6
00:48:18.706 --> 00:48:23.666
You know, the church has been saying this since I was just growing up in the church.

7
00:48:23.666 --> 00:48:26.106
I was born in the church, I would say.

8
00:48:26.106 --> 00:48:30.266
And back in the 80s and 90s, we always said that during Easter.

9
00:48:30.266 --> 00:48:32.546
The Lord is truly risen.

10
00:48:32.546 --> 00:48:36.146
And it becomes a bit of a cliché, you know, throughout your life.

11
00:48:36.146 --> 00:48:38.626
But it's only a cliché because it's true.

12
00:48:38.666 --> 00:48:42.306
The Lord is truly risen. Amen.

13
00:48:42.306 --> 00:48:44.626
Is everyone happy in the room?

14
00:48:44.626 --> 00:48:50.786
Praise God. Today we are baptizing eleven people in the name of Jesus.

15
00:48:50.786 --> 00:48:52.266
Eleven people.

16
00:48:56.266 --> 00:49:02.026
Wonderful. Praise God. Today there is celebration in heaven.

17
00:49:02.066 --> 00:49:09.186
The Bible says that when one person comes to Christ, the angels in heaven rejoice.

18
00:49:09.186 --> 00:49:11.586
One person. One person.

19
00:49:11.586 --> 00:49:15.306
Today we are baptizing eleven people in the name of King Jesus.

20
00:49:15.306 --> 00:49:19.826
And I am sure there is joy in heaven, but there is also joy in the church. Amen.

21
00:49:19.826 --> 00:49:21.826
Amen.

22
00:49:21.826 --> 00:49:29.186
I invite Bram to the stage and Bram is going to talk about the collections, about the money from Open Church.

23
00:49:29.226 --> 00:49:31.186
And about what the people give in Open Church.

24
00:49:31.186 --> 00:49:39.186
And I want to make it clear, if Open Church is your home, if you call this your home church, then this message is for you.

25
00:49:39.186 --> 00:49:45.386
If you are visiting here today, if you are family or friends of one of the baptized,

26
00:49:45.386 --> 00:49:48.146
feel free to participate and listen in,

27
00:49:48.146 --> 00:49:52.906
but this is really a message to the people as the family of Open Church.

28
00:49:52.906 --> 00:49:54.546
Do you understand what I mean?

29
00:49:54.546 --> 00:49:56.026
Thanks.

30
00:49:56.026 --> 00:49:58.026
Thank you very much.

31
00:49:58.026 --> 00:50:00.026
Good morning.

32
00:50:00.026 --> 00:50:06.026
As we know as a church, we are working on a construction project.

33
00:50:06.026 --> 00:50:14.026
And behind me are a few large drawings that indicate what it is going to look like.

34
00:50:14.026 --> 00:50:24.026
And for that construction project, we held an extensive information evening some time ago.

35
00:50:25.026 --> 00:50:38.026
And there we explained that it greatly helps for the financing if we arrange some loans from our own church together.

36
00:50:38.026 --> 00:50:50.026
People have signed up for that and so far there have been commitments for 170,000.

37
00:50:55.026 --> 00:50:58.026
That is fantastic.

38
00:50:58.026 --> 00:51:02.026
The goal is 400,000.

39
00:51:02.026 --> 00:51:10.026
If we have that, then we have a strong story to someone who can finance a long-term mortgage, to a financier for that.

40
00:51:10.026 --> 00:51:13.026
So we are not there yet.

41
00:51:13.026 --> 00:51:23.026
We have also heard from various people that the deadline to register was actually quite short.

42
00:51:24.026 --> 00:51:30.026
And for that reason, we say that you can register until May 1.

43
00:51:30.026 --> 00:51:32.026
So we are changing that now.

44
00:51:32.026 --> 00:51:35.026
It is possible to register for the loan until May 1.

45
00:51:35.026 --> 00:51:40.026
After that, it is still possible, but we cannot include it in the plan.

46
00:51:40.026 --> 00:51:48.026
At some point, we need to have the plan on paper and send it to potential funders.

47
00:51:49.026 --> 00:51:52.026
Until May 1.

48
00:51:52.026 --> 00:51:56.026
I will be on that side of the stage after the service.

49
00:51:56.026 --> 00:51:59.026
Questions are always welcome.

50
00:51:59.026 --> 00:52:04.026
Questions via email are also possible, bram.openkerk.com.

51
00:52:04.026 --> 00:52:06.026
We couldn't make it any simpler.

52
00:52:06.026 --> 00:52:08.026
I will be there.

53
00:52:08.026 --> 00:52:13.026
Questions, submitting cards, all of that is possible.

54
00:52:13.026 --> 00:52:17.026
May I have the slide?

55
00:52:18.026 --> 00:52:21.026
Yes.

56
00:52:21.026 --> 00:52:23.026
This is once again a summary.

57
00:52:23.026 --> 00:52:27.026
Of course, you are lending money to the church.

58
00:52:27.026 --> 00:52:29.026
That can be with interest or without interest.

59
00:52:29.026 --> 00:52:30.026
We offer two options.

60
00:52:30.026 --> 00:52:32.026
The term will be 6 years.

61
00:52:32.026 --> 00:52:37.026
Of course only if you do not need that money during that period.

62
00:52:37.026 --> 00:52:40.026
You have to be very sober-minded.

63
00:52:40.026 --> 00:52:47.026
And please provide your name, your email, the amount, and whether you want to borrow without interest.

64
00:52:51.026 --> 00:52:54.026
And this is the core.

65
00:52:54.026 --> 00:52:59.026
These commitments testify to willingness.

66
00:52:59.026 --> 00:53:01.026
People who want to participate.

67
00:53:01.026 --> 00:53:04.026
People who want to bear the burden together.

68
00:53:04.026 --> 00:53:06.026
People who...

69
00:53:06.026 --> 00:53:07.026
Yes.

70
00:53:07.026 --> 00:53:10.026
But also people who have the means.

71
00:53:10.026 --> 00:53:14.026
For when the willingness is present, that is a good thing.

72
00:53:14.026 --> 00:53:17.026
Then it is welcome according to what she has.

73
00:53:17.026 --> 00:53:21.026
And not according to what she does not have.

74
00:53:21.026 --> 00:53:27.026
This is, and maybe if you are here as a guest, you suddenly say, where am I falling into now?

75
00:53:27.026 --> 00:53:31.026
This is the fundamental attitude that we find healthy.

76
00:53:31.026 --> 00:53:33.026
This is what the Bible teaches us.

77
00:53:33.026 --> 00:53:36.026
Willingness is fantastic.

78
00:53:36.026 --> 00:53:39.026
But we do not have to give from what we do not have.

79
00:53:39.026 --> 00:53:41.026
We give from what we have.

80
00:53:41.026 --> 00:53:45.026
We give according to what is in our heart.

81
00:53:45.026 --> 00:53:48.026
Just checking, because I had...

82
00:53:48.026 --> 00:53:50.026
Yes, exactly.

83
00:53:50.026 --> 00:53:55.026
I wanted to make sure that I said everything I planned to say.

84
00:53:55.026 --> 00:53:57.026
That is the construction project.

85
00:53:57.026 --> 00:54:00.026
The collection today is just for the church.

86
00:54:00.026 --> 00:54:02.026
Just for the... just.

87
00:54:02.026 --> 00:54:07.026
Just for the fantastic daily functioning of our own church.

88
00:54:07.026 --> 00:54:10.026
As usual, we can give via the app.

89
00:54:10.026 --> 00:54:12.026
We can give via the bank.

90
00:54:12.026 --> 00:54:14.026
We have QR codes for that.

91
00:54:14.026 --> 00:54:16.026
There is a card on many chairs.

92
00:54:16.026 --> 00:54:19.026
Guests, please do not feel obligated.

93
00:54:19.026 --> 00:54:23.026
But if you say I'm in, of course, you are also welcome.

94
00:54:23.026 --> 00:54:25.026
Thank you.

95
00:54:33.026 --> 00:54:37.026
Yes. We are going to start with the Word of God. Amen.

96
00:54:41.026 --> 00:54:43.026
Hallelujah.

97
00:54:43.026 --> 00:54:47.026
Soon we will baptize eleven people in the name of Jesus.

98
00:54:47.026 --> 00:54:51.026
And at the same time, today is resurrection Sunday.

99
00:54:51.026 --> 00:54:55.026
And as a church, we have chosen to...

100
00:54:56.026 --> 00:55:00.026
...to combine these two things.

101
00:55:00.026 --> 00:55:04.026
For example, we could have celebrated Resurrection Sunday today.

102
00:55:04.026 --> 00:55:07.026
And then we could have celebrated the baptism service next week.

103
00:55:07.026 --> 00:55:12.026
So that we can give a lot of attention to Easter today.

104
00:55:12.026 --> 00:55:15.026
That Jesus Christ rose from the dead.

105
00:55:15.026 --> 00:55:20.026
And then we could fully focus next week on the fact...

106
00:55:20.026 --> 00:55:23.026
...that people are getting baptized in the name of Jesus.

107
00:55:23.026 --> 00:55:26.026
But I want to combine both.

108
00:55:26.026 --> 00:55:30.026
Because essentially being baptized in the name of Jesus today...

109
00:55:30.026 --> 00:55:34.026
...is an ultimate opportunity to celebrate...

110
00:55:34.026 --> 00:55:38.026
...that Jesus Christ died on a cross for your and my sin.

111
00:55:38.026 --> 00:55:41.026
But three days later he rose from the dead.

112
00:55:41.026 --> 00:55:46.026
And Carolien just stopped reading from Matthew chapter 28.

113
00:55:46.026 --> 00:55:49.026
Because in Matthew chapter 28 it says that part...

114
00:55:49.026 --> 00:55:53.026
...or in chapter 27 it says that part that Jesus rose from the dead.

115
00:55:53.026 --> 00:55:56.026
And the women fell at his feet...

116
00:55:56.026 --> 00:55:59.026
...to feel that he was really there in worship.

117
00:55:59.026 --> 00:56:02.026
They felt his hands and they felt his feet...

118
00:56:02.026 --> 00:56:07.026
...to prove that Jesus physically rose from the dead.

119
00:56:07.026 --> 00:56:10.026
Dear church, I want to say one thing to you in advance.

120
00:56:10.026 --> 00:56:17.026
We do not believe in some kind of mirage.

121
00:56:18.026 --> 00:56:21.026
That one or another hope that we have of...

122
00:56:21.026 --> 00:56:25.026
...what a shame that Jesus was such a good man that he ultimately was killed.

123
00:56:25.026 --> 00:56:29.026
And his ideas live on and on.

124
00:56:29.026 --> 00:56:32.026
No, it is not an idea in which we believe.

125
00:56:32.026 --> 00:56:35.026
It is not a philosophy that can continue on.

126
00:56:35.026 --> 00:56:39.026
The philosophy of feel good and grace and forgiveness.

127
00:56:39.026 --> 00:56:42.026
No, we do not believe in a philosophy.

128
00:56:42.026 --> 00:56:44.026
We do not believe in a tradition.

129
00:56:44.026 --> 00:56:47.026
We do not believe in a feel good moment.

130
00:56:47.026 --> 00:56:50.026
We believe in a physically risen man.

131
00:56:50.026 --> 00:56:55.026
His name is Jesus. He is the Messiah. He is the Christ.

132
00:56:56.026 --> 00:57:02.026
And so to prove that he rose in a physical body...

133
00:57:02.026 --> 00:57:04.026
...he let them feel his hands and his feet.

134
00:57:04.026 --> 00:57:08.026
And the people could feel the holes and the scars...

135
00:57:08.026 --> 00:57:10.026
...of what had happened.

136
00:57:10.026 --> 00:57:15.026
And to further prove that he truly was who he was...

137
00:57:15.026 --> 00:57:17.026
...he said at one point, and I love that moment...

138
00:57:17.026 --> 00:57:20.026
...he said, I am hungry. I know that feeling.

139
00:57:20.026 --> 00:57:24.026
And then he says, I am hungry. Do you perhaps have something to eat?

140
00:57:24.026 --> 00:57:26.026
And his disciples were really like...

141
00:57:27.026 --> 00:57:32.026
Okay, here you have fish and honey. And he ate where they were present.

142
00:57:32.026 --> 00:57:35.026
I love it. A wedding meal awaits us.

143
00:57:35.026 --> 00:57:37.026
For the story is not over yet.

144
00:57:37.026 --> 00:57:42.026
Jesus rose from the dead. He made himself felt as to who he truly was.

145
00:57:42.026 --> 00:57:46.026
He ate fish and he ate honey to prove that it was a real human...

146
00:57:46.026 --> 00:57:48.026
...who has risen from the dead.

147
00:57:48.026 --> 00:57:51.026
But the story doesn't stop there. The story continues.

148
00:57:51.026 --> 00:57:56.026
For Jesus went to the Father. He is praying for you personally at this moment.

149
00:57:56.026 --> 00:58:00.026
Not only for the people who are sitting here and who are being baptized there.

150
00:58:00.026 --> 00:58:04.026
But the Bible teaches that Jesus Christ now, through what he has done...

151
00:58:04.026 --> 00:58:08.026
...possesses all highest honor and glory in himself...

152
00:58:08.026 --> 00:58:12.026
...because he is now seated at the right hand of the throne of God.

153
00:58:12.026 --> 00:58:15.026
And do you know what he is doing there? He is praying for you.

154
00:58:15.026 --> 00:58:20.026
He is praying for you. What an amazing Lord we have.

155
00:58:20.026 --> 00:58:21.026
Praise God.

156
00:58:21.026 --> 00:58:25.026
And I want to give attention to that resurrection.

157
00:58:25.026 --> 00:58:28.026
I want to give attention to today being Easter.

158
00:58:28.026 --> 00:58:32.026
And I could easily talk about that for an hour or two, three, four.

159
00:58:32.026 --> 00:58:33.026
Only the resurrection.

160
00:58:33.026 --> 00:58:37.026
And at the same time, I also want to baptize people in the name of Jesus.

161
00:58:37.026 --> 00:58:40.026
For the moment you have been baptized in Jesus' name...

162
00:58:40.026 --> 00:58:43.026
...that moment is everything taken away from you.

163
00:58:43.026 --> 00:58:47.026
You have received a new life. You have received a mantle of righteousness.

164
00:58:47.026 --> 00:58:50.026
And you are forever written in the book of the Father.

165
00:58:50.026 --> 00:58:53.026
You are completely His now.

166
00:58:53.026 --> 00:58:57.026
Through the baptismal water of Jesus Christ. And we will also pay attention to that.

167
00:58:57.026 --> 00:59:00.026
And I thought to myself, how are we going to do that?

168
00:59:00.026 --> 00:59:03.026
In one moment, ha! Thank you, Paul.

169
00:59:03.026 --> 00:59:05.026
For Paul wrote about that.

170
00:59:05.026 --> 00:59:12.026
Paul wrote about the meaning of the resurrection of Jesus Christ.

171
00:59:12.026 --> 00:59:15.026
And what baptism has to do with it.

172
00:59:15.026 --> 00:59:21.026
Now, at one point, Paul wrote a letter to the church in Rome.

173
00:59:21.026 --> 00:59:24.026
Paul was not a pastor there.

174
00:59:24.026 --> 00:59:27.026
He had actually very little to do with this church.

175
00:59:27.026 --> 00:59:30.026
But Paul found out that there was conflict in the church in Rome.

176
00:59:30.026 --> 00:59:34.026
For there were people who had been believers for a long time.

177
00:59:34.026 --> 00:59:35.026
The Jews.

178
00:59:35.026 --> 00:59:38.026
And there were also people who had been believers for a shorter time.

179
00:59:38.026 --> 00:59:40.026
And those were non-Jewish Christians.

180
00:59:40.026 --> 00:59:42.026
They were the Greek Christians.

181
00:59:42.026 --> 00:59:44.026
Those were the non-Jewish Christians.

182
00:59:44.026 --> 00:59:46.026
They are also sometimes called the Gentiles.

183
00:59:46.026 --> 00:59:49.026
But well, let's stick to the non-Jewish Christians.

184
00:59:49.026 --> 00:59:51.026
Let's stick to the Greeks.

185
00:59:51.026 --> 00:59:54.026
And Paul heard that there was a dispute.

186
00:59:54.026 --> 01:00:00.026
For the gospel, that is the good news that Jesus has risen.

187
01:00:00.026 --> 01:00:01.026
Hallelujah, amen.

188
01:00:01.026 --> 01:00:06.026
The good news that Jesus has risen is good news for you and for me.

189
01:00:06.026 --> 01:00:10.026
And for the people 2000 years ago in the church in Rome.

190
01:00:10.026 --> 01:00:15.026
But that good news was not well understood because of that dispute.

191
01:00:15.026 --> 01:00:17.026
For the people started to form a little church.

192
01:00:17.026 --> 01:00:20.026
And in the church were the Jewish Christians.

193
01:00:20.026 --> 01:00:22.026
And they said, you must behave like this.

194
01:00:22.026 --> 01:00:23.026
And this is how it is.

195
01:00:23.026 --> 01:00:25.026
And this is how you should behave.

196
01:00:25.026 --> 01:00:27.026
And then you had the Greek Christians who said,

197
01:00:27.026 --> 01:00:29.026
well, we don't really know what you have to say about that.

198
01:00:29.026 --> 01:00:31.026
And all your traditions.

199
01:00:31.026 --> 01:00:32.026
And all your law.

200
01:00:32.026 --> 01:00:34.026
We find all of that quite strange.

201
01:00:34.026 --> 01:00:36.026
And there arose a dispute.

202
01:00:36.026 --> 01:00:40.026
And Paul thought to himself, yes I may not be the pastor of that church.

203
01:00:40.026 --> 01:00:44.026
But if I don't do something about this, that church will fall apart immediately.

204
01:00:44.026 --> 01:00:46.026
Then all the work will have been in vain.

205
01:00:46.026 --> 01:00:49.026
So Paul writes a letter.

206
01:00:49.026 --> 01:00:51.026
The letter to the Romans.

207
01:00:51.026 --> 01:00:57.026
And the letter to the Romans is actually the entire Bible explained in one short letter.

208
01:00:57.026 --> 01:01:00.026
You can read that letter in one afternoon.

209
01:01:00.026 --> 01:01:04.026
And Paul actually writes down what it is really about in that letter to the Romans.

210
01:01:04.026 --> 01:01:09.026
I want to advise you, if you have a few hours, go through that letter to the Romans.

211
01:01:09.026 --> 01:01:10.026
Wonderful.

212
01:01:10.026 --> 01:01:14.026
And I want to explain with three verses, three lessons

213
01:01:14.026 --> 01:01:19.026
about what the resurrection of Jesus Christ really means.

214
01:01:19.026 --> 01:01:24.026
For what does it matter to me in 2025 that Jesus rose from the dead?

215
01:01:24.026 --> 01:01:26.026
I am glad you asked.

216
01:01:26.026 --> 01:01:32.026
Lesson 1. The resurrection of Jesus proves that Jesus is God.

217
01:01:33.026 --> 01:01:38.026
The resurrection of Jesus proves that He Himself is God.

218
01:01:39.026 --> 01:01:41.026
For who created everything? God.

219
01:01:41.026 --> 01:01:44.026
Who is the creator of heaven and earth? God.

220
01:01:44.026 --> 01:01:46.026
Who gave life? God.

221
01:01:46.026 --> 01:01:49.026
Who can give life and who can take life?

222
01:01:49.026 --> 01:01:50.026
Only God.

223
01:01:51.026 --> 01:01:57.026
And you know, in the Bible there were also people, like for example Elijah,

224
01:01:57.026 --> 01:02:02.026
who once was able to bring someone back from the dead.

225
01:02:02.026 --> 01:02:06.026
But Jesus, according to the Bible, is the first,

226
01:02:06.026 --> 01:02:09.026
the firstborn, is a bit of a difficult term,

227
01:02:09.026 --> 01:02:14.026
but Jesus is the first who laid down his life.

228
01:02:14.026 --> 01:02:19.026
The Bible says, no one killed Him, He gave His life on the cross.

229
01:02:19.026 --> 01:02:21.026
That is a big difference.

230
01:02:21.026 --> 01:02:25.026
They did not kill Jesus, He gave His life for you and me.

231
01:02:25.026 --> 01:02:29.026
And He is the first who laid down His life on the cross

232
01:02:29.026 --> 01:02:36.026
and He is also the only one who could rise again on His own initiative and by His own power.

233
01:02:36.026 --> 01:02:40.026
And that is the proof that you are of divine order.

234
01:02:40.026 --> 01:02:42.026
That is the proof that you are God Himself.

235
01:02:42.026 --> 01:02:45.026
The Bible says in Romans chapter 1, verses 3 to 4,

236
01:02:45.026 --> 01:02:47.026
we have it here on the screen,

237
01:02:47.026 --> 01:02:51.026
the good news is about the Son.

238
01:02:51.026 --> 01:02:54.026
The good news is about the Son.

239
01:02:54.026 --> 01:03:00.026
The Son was born as a man from the family of which king?

240
01:03:00.026 --> 01:03:03.026
I believe we are dealing with this this year, about this David.

241
01:03:03.026 --> 01:03:05.026
Great that this is here.

242
01:03:05.026 --> 01:03:09.026
The Son was born as a man from the family of King David.

243
01:03:09.026 --> 01:03:14.026
Jesus was killed, but the Holy Spirit raised Jesus back to life.

244
01:03:14.026 --> 01:03:16.026
Can I get an amen on that?

245
01:03:16.026 --> 01:03:18.026
With this, pay close attention to these words,

